messages.content:
In all the world, none dearer than a mother;
No peace on earth is like her, and no other.
When age has come to settle on her frame,
Stand by her, cypress-tall, and guard her name.
Speak gently, and make glad her waiting heart;
With calls and visits, never be apart.
Say: "Heart and soul and body, all from you";
And thank her in each gathering, loud and true.
